# Cross-client fixtures are byte-exact contracts shared with gov5: their
# SHA-256 is pinned on both sides. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites them to CRLF, which changes those bytes and makes the pinned-SHA
# tests report drift that does not exist. gov5 pins the same attribute for the
# same reason; keep the two in step.
crates/n42-network/testdata/*.json -text
crates/n42-consensus-service/testdata/*.json -text
